!Mamool Ja Training Grounds.jpg|right|Mamool Ja Training Grounds
=2 Walkthrough
The objective of this assault is to return at least 1 gem to the start NPC, {n:Zahakahm}. While it is very easy to win this assault, it is very difficult to maximize AP return due to the mechanics of the assault, which is built like a game of tag.
* The Mamool Ja Savage's team is comprised of:
** {n:Mamool Ja Governor}
** {n:Red Badge Mamool Ja}
** {n:Blue Badge Mamool Ja}
** {n:Yellow Badge Mamool Ja}
** {n:Green Badge Mamool Ja}
** {n:White Badge Mamool Ja}
** {n:Black Badge Mamool Ja}

* Gems can be found in coffers scattered about the map.
* When you are carrying a gem you are vulnerable to be "tagged" by Mamool Ja.
* When tagged, the Mamool Ja will take your gem and you will respawn at the start NPC.
* When you are not carrying a gem, you can tag a Mamool Ja who is carrying a gem.
* When you tag a Mamool Ja, you will take its gem and it will respawn at F-7 where their base and NPC {n:Mamool Ja Governor} are.
* Speaking to the NPC {n:Mamool Ja Governor} will return you to the starting point and cause a gem you hold to be taken.
* Zone-wide information will be given whenever a jewel is obtained, stolen, or returned to each teams NPC.

Once all the gems are returned to either your base or the Mamool Ja base a zone message states "You have recovered all the treasure". Speak to the start NPC {n:Zahakahm} at any point after returning at least 1 gem to spawn the Rune of Release.{br} Base AP is calculated as 200 + 133 per gem returned. It is not currently known how many gems there are, however data suggests 9 Coffers total.
